+        // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+        // [ff9mapkit netsync B5] stage 6 -- THE GUEST'S EXIT WITH THE HOST (studies/battle-coop/B4-B5-DESIGN.md 5.4; section 7,
+        // stage 6). Until this stage a guest that presented the host's end held black at the WAIT seq (R8 refusing) until the
+        // watcher's stale-lane leave -- ~2 s after the host was already back on its field, because the host's type-1 lane stays
+        // live through its whole result screen (design 3.6). Now:
+        //   THE TRIGGER -- this boot's end block (the bench seam's, or BootedWireNonce's) names the host's exit: ui 1 + ResultState
+        //     Hide (its last result Confirm, or InitialNone's 0.3 s exit), ui 2 (Game Over) or ui 3 (the title) --
+        //     NetSyncEnd.HostExitTrigger. It LATCHES once per boot (the lane may go stale a moment later), closes the B4 stock
+        //     menu and stops any further presentation (a late boot that never presented just follows the host out).
+        //   THE END-LEAVE -- Leave() at most once per second (NetSyncEnd.ExitVerdict): never while a leave is already in flight
+        //     (ours, a ~ press, the watcher's: none is stolen or double-issued), never into a scene fade (Leave would only
+        //     defer -- design 3.8 item 2 -- so the deferral is counted and logged ONCE instead of Leave's per-call line). The
+        //     teardown then stamps the watcher's skip nonce through its "leave noted" branch (NetSyncClient), so the same
+        //     fight never re-boots (two-machine only: a selftest boot has no wire nonce -- design 3.8 item 3).
+        //   THE RETURN SETTLE -- any Leave of a FINISHED fight (the end-leave; a ~ press on the black hold; the watcher's
+        //     stale-lane leave after an AfterEvent screen, which never shows Hide), once per boot, does what the stock result
