+        //     onto the field (skipped while the host -- end-block flag b4 -- or the guest keeps its field song,
+        //     BTL_CONTI_FLD_SONG); then at the TEARDOWN, after the last battle frame and before the return's StartEvents, the
+        //     host's btl_result is stamped (NetSyncEnd.StampFor: NO_POSE -> VICTORY, GAMEOVER / INITIAL never, and a DEFEAT
+        //     outside a NoGameOver scene never -- it is a Game Over in transit) and, when this boot INJECTED an end, the end
+        //     fade is lifted the stock way: FF9Wipe_FadeInEx(256), the result screen's own hide tail. The injected
+        //     FF9Wipe_FadeOutEx(32) is a shader subtract that nothing on a field undoes (ServiceFade stops once its frame target
+        //     is passed) [I], so without the lift the return could render black.
+        //     The stamp the Leave decides is PROVISIONAL: a manual leave can land while the host's result is not final yet (a
